  "coupleChallenge1Title": "Recreating your first date",
  "coupleChallenge1Description": "Go back to where it all began.\n\nTry to recreate the little details: the food, the clothes, the phrases, the nerves.\n\nTalk about who you were back then and how much you have grown together.\n\nIt will be impossible not to laugh at old memories and feel grateful for everything you have lived.",
  "coupleChallenge1Motivation": "Sometimes the best way to see how far you have come is to go back to the beginning.",
  "coupleChallenge1Category": "Experiential",
  "coupleChallenge1Location": "Outdoors",
  "coupleChallenge1Timing": "Anytime",
  "coupleChallenge2Title": "Candlelight dinner",
  "coupleChallenge2Description": "All you need is a few candles or warm lights, a meal, and something delicious to drink.\n\nTurn off the lights, slow down, and let the silence fill with soft music and long looks.\n\nThe menu does not matter as much as the presence of the person in front of you.",
  "coupleChallenge2Motivation": "A perfect date to reconnect without distractions and remember why you choose each other every day.",
  "coupleChallenge2Category": "Romantic",
  "coupleChallenge2Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge2Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge3Title": "Shared dream list",
  "coupleChallenge3Description": "Grab paper and a pen. Write down at least 10 things you would love to achieve together as a couple: trips, goals, or dreams.\n\nRead them out loud to each other and keep the list as a reminder.",
  "coupleChallenge3Motivation": "Shared dreams do not just bring you closer. They also give your story direction.",
  "coupleChallenge3Category": "Emotional",
  "coupleChallenge3Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge3Timing": "Afternoon",
  "coupleChallenge4Title": "Home karaoke",
  "coupleChallenge4Description": "Turn the volume up, pick your songs, and let the fun begin. You do not need a microphone or a perfect voice, just attitude.\n\nBetween laughs, you will discover how freeing it is to laugh together.",
  "coupleChallenge4Motivation": "Love can be off-key too, as long as you are singing to the same rhythm.",
  "coupleChallenge4Category": "Playful",
  "coupleChallenge4Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge4Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge5Title": "Painting together",
  "coupleChallenge5Description": "Get some paper and brushes. It does not matter if you do not know how to draw. The idea is to let your mind go, laugh at the lines, and enjoy the color.\n\nPaint something that represents you as a couple.",
  "coupleChallenge5Motivation": "Art is not looking for perfection. It is looking for connection.",
  "coupleChallenge5Category": "Creative",
  "coupleChallenge5Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge5Timing": "Flexible",
  "coupleChallenge6Title": "Movie marathon",
  "coupleChallenge6Description": "Create your own little cinema: dim lights, blankets, snacks, and a list of movies chosen by both of you.\n\nWatching movies together is also about side glances and laughing in sync.",
  "coupleChallenge6Motivation": "Little things are often what make love feel big.",
  "coupleChallenge6Category": "Relaxed",
  "coupleChallenge6Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge6Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge7Title": "Photo walk",
  "coupleChallenge7Description": "Go out for a walk without a plan and try to capture what usually goes unnoticed: a shadow, a smile, a reflection.\n\nTake pictures of whatever makes you stop.",
  "coupleChallenge7Motivation": "Sometimes seeing the world through a lens is the best way to look at each other again.",
  "coupleChallenge7Category": "Adventure",
  "coupleChallenge7Location": "City",
  "coupleChallenge7Timing": "Afternoon",
  "coupleChallenge8Title": "Spontaneous picnic",
  "coupleChallenge8Description": "A blanket, a few snacks, cold drinks, and a desire to share the moment.\n\nFind a park, a square, or even your backyard, settle in, and let the conversation flow.\n\nAdd a card game, a book, or simply stare at the sky together.",
  "coupleChallenge8Motivation": "You do not have to go far to feel like you escaped the world together.",
  "coupleChallenge8Category": "Experiential",
  "coupleChallenge8Location": "Outdoors",
  "coupleChallenge8Timing": "Afternoon",
  "coupleChallenge9Title": "Letters that do not disappear",
  "coupleChallenge9Description": "Write each other a letter. Not on your phone, with paper and ink.\n\nPut on soft music, make something tasty, and let yourselves drift.\n\nWrite what you admire, what you are grateful for, and what you dream about.\n\nAt the end, exchange them and read them out loud.",
  "coupleChallenge9Motivation": "Letters stay, words can be reread, but what lasts the most is how they make you feel.",
  "coupleChallenge9Category": "Emotional",
  "coupleChallenge9Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge9Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge10Title": "Total disconnect",
  "coupleChallenge10Description": "Turn off your phones, the TV, and every outside notification for one night.\n\nRead, cook, talk, play, or simply hold each other without interruptions.\n\nYou will discover that when digital noise fades, a different kind of silence appears: the one that makes room for presence.",
  "coupleChallenge10Motivation": "This date is not measured in minutes, but in real connection.",
  "coupleChallenge10Category": "Emotional",
  "coupleChallenge10Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge10Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge11Title": "Jar of questions",
  "coupleChallenge11Description": "Fill a jar with little slips of paper containing funny or deep questions.\n\n\"What was the first thing you thought when you met me?\" or \"What dream have you still not dared to tell me about?\"\n\nDraw them at random and answer without filters. You will end up somewhere between laughter and long gazes.",
  "coupleChallenge11Motivation": "Some conversations do not appear until you invite them in.",
  "coupleChallenge11Category": "Playful",
  "coupleChallenge11Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge11Timing": "Anytime",
  "coupleChallenge23Title": "Breakfast with a view",
  "coupleChallenge23Description": "Change the setting of breakfast: make something delicious and go find a view. It can be a park, a rooftop, or a bench in a square.\n\nTake the time to enjoy the fresh air and coffee without checking the clock.",
  "coupleChallenge23Motivation": "Coffee tastes better when the horizon is the limit.",
  "coupleChallenge23Category": "Exploration",
  "coupleChallenge23Location": "Outdoors",
  "coupleChallenge23Timing": "Morning",
  "coupleChallenge24Title": "At the edge of the world",
  "coupleChallenge24Description": "Pick a place where the horizon feels endless: a shore, a river, or a lagoon. Bring something to sit on and simply watch the sun go down.\n\nWrite a note together about what you dream of and save it for the future.",
  "coupleChallenge24Motivation": "Shared silence in front of water can say more than a thousand words.",
  "coupleChallenge24Category": "Emotional",
  "coupleChallenge24Location": "Nature",
  "coupleChallenge24Timing": "Sunset",
  "coupleChallenge25Title": "Unknown destination",
  "coupleChallenge25Description": "Go for a walk without a map or GPS. Pick a direction at random and every five blocks one of you decides where to turn.\n\nDiscover new corners of your city as if you were lost tourists.",
  "coupleChallenge25Motivation": "Getting lost together is one of the best ways to find each other.",
  "coupleChallenge25Category": "Exploration",
  "coupleChallenge25Location": "City",
  "coupleChallenge25Timing": "Afternoon",
  "coupleChallenge26Title": "Present-moment ritual",
  "coupleChallenge26Description": "Create a space with warm light and soft music. Each of you writes down three things you want to leave behind, like fears or anger, and three things you are grateful for in the other person.\n\nBurn what you want to let go of and keep the gratitude notes in a jar.",
  "coupleChallenge26Motivation": "Clearing the past makes room for a brighter future.",
  "coupleChallenge26Category": "Emotional",
  "coupleChallenge26Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge26Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge27Title": "Architect of surprises",
  "coupleChallenge27Description": "One of you plans a small surprise: a note on the pillow, a favorite meal prepared in secret, or a tiny clue leading to a little adventure.\n\nThe key is the mystery and the detail that was thought through for the other person only.",
  "coupleChallenge27Motivation": "Love lives in the details that say \"I was thinking of you.\"",
  "coupleChallenge27Category": "Thoughtful",
  "coupleChallenge27Location": "Anywhere",
  "coupleChallenge27Timing": "Surprise",
  "coupleChallenge28Title": "In the service of love",
  "coupleChallenge28Description": "Take turns \"taking care\" of the other for a while: prepare a bath, give a massage, or cook while the other person does absolutely nothing.\n\nThis is not about serving. It is about caring with tenderness and intention.",
  "coupleChallenge28Motivation": "Caring is one of the quietest and strongest ways to love.",
  "coupleChallenge28Category": "Everyday",
  "coupleChallenge28Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge28Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge29Title": "Stories on stage",
  "coupleChallenge29Description": "Pick a famous scene from a movie and try to recreate it with whatever you have at home. Do not aim for perfection, aim for laughter and complicity.\n\nAt the end, invent your own ending together.",
  "coupleChallenge29Motivation": "Pretending to be someone else can help you rediscover who you are together.",
  "coupleChallenge29Category": "Playful",
  "coupleChallenge29Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge29Timing": "Anytime",
  "coupleChallenge30Title": "Flavors with a story",
  "coupleChallenge30Description": "Choose three flavors such as wine, chocolate, or cheese, and for each one share a personal memory connected to it: a trip, childhood, or a person.\n\nLet taste awaken stories you still have not told each other.",
  "coupleChallenge30Motivation": "Every bite can open a door to a memory.",
  "coupleChallenge30Category": "Experiential",
  "coupleChallenge30Location": "Anywhere",
  "coupleChallenge30Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge31Title": "The art of doing nothing",
  "coupleChallenge31Description": "Turn off alarms and forget the to-do list. Spend a day without schedules: read in bed, watch old shows, or talk without a destination.\n\nGive yourselves the luxury of inhabiting time without the pressure to be productive.",
  "coupleChallenge31Motivation": "Time \"wasted\" together is time gained in connection.",
  "coupleChallenge31Category": "Relaxed",
  "coupleChallenge31Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge31Timing": "All day",
  "coupleChallenge32Title": "Market Sunday",
  "coupleChallenge32Description": "Go to a local market with cloth bags and mate. Do not focus on buying a lot. Focus on the colors, the smells, and the people.\n\nChoose one unusual ingredient to cook something new when you get back home.",
  "coupleChallenge32Motivation": "Routine can have its own handmade kind of magic.",
  "coupleChallenge32Category": "Exploration",
  "coupleChallenge32Location": "City",
  "coupleChallenge32Timing": "Morning",
  "coupleChallenge33Title": "Under the stars",
  "coupleChallenge33Description": "Find a spot away from city lights. Bring a blanket, open sky, and silence.\n\nCount stars, invent your own constellations, or simply feel the immensity together.",
  "coupleChallenge33Motivation": "The whole universe fits in the space between the two of you.",
  "coupleChallenge33Category": "Romantic",
  "coupleChallenge33Location": "Nature",
  "coupleChallenge33Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge34Title": "Night of the senses",
  "coupleChallenge34Description": "Set a table with mysterious textures, aromas, and flavors. With eyes closed, the other person has to guess what they are feeling.\n\nA dynamic meant to surrender to sensation without needing many words.",
  "coupleChallenge34Motivation": "Love can be tasted, smelled, and touched.",
  "coupleChallenge34Category": "Sensory",
  "coupleChallenge34Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge34Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge35Title": "Shared reading",
  "coupleChallenge35Description": "Choose a book, poem, or article and read it out loud, taking turns with each section. Listen to each other's tone and pauses.\n\nWhen you finish, share what the story made you think or feel.",
  "coupleChallenge35Motivation": "Words are a bridge between two minds.",
  "coupleChallenge35Category": "Intellectual",
  "coupleChallenge35Location": "Quiet place",
  "coupleChallenge35Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge36Title": "Micro-theater date",
  "coupleChallenge36Description": "Find a micro-theater performance or a short play. Experience the intensity of a story that feels close and alive.\n\nThen take a walk while talking about what made you laugh, cry, or reflect.",
  "coupleChallenge36Motivation": "Living a thousand lives in one night, always hand in hand.",
  "coupleChallenge36Category": "Cultural",
  "coupleChallenge36Location": "City",
  "coupleChallenge36Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge37Title": "Trip without luggage",
  "coupleChallenge37Description": "Choose a country and turn your home into that destination for one night: typical food, music, and atmosphere from that place.\n\nTravel without a passport and imagine what you would do if you were really there.",
  "coupleChallenge37Motivation": "The best destination is the one you create between the two of you.",
  "coupleChallenge37Category": "Creative",
  "coupleChallenge37Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge37Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge38Title": "The secret envelope",
  "coupleChallenge38Description": "One of you prepares three envelopes with instructions to open in stages: an outfit, a meeting place, and a special ending.\n\nThe magic is in the anticipation of not knowing what comes next.",
  "coupleChallenge38Motivation": "Every envelope is an \"I thought of you\" waiting to be opened.",
  "coupleChallenge38Category": "Adventure",
  "coupleChallenge38Location": "Surprise",
  "coupleChallenge38Timing": "All afternoon",
  "coupleChallenge39Title": "Promises at dawn",
  "coupleChallenge39Description": "Go somewhere high enough to watch the sun rise. When the first ray appears, promise one small thing for your relationship.\n\nA habit, a wish, or a change you want to begin with the new day.",
  "coupleChallenge39Motivation": "Every sunrise is a chance to begin again.",
  "coupleChallenge39Category": "Emotional",
  "coupleChallenge39Location": "Outdoors",
  "coupleChallenge39Timing": "Dawn",
  "coupleChallenge40Title": "Building patience",
  "coupleChallenge40Description": "Spend the afternoon putting together a puzzle side by side, with mate or wine nearby.\n\nBetween pieces, let calm conversations and comfortable silence flow.",
  "coupleChallenge40Motivation": "Putting together small things is practice for the patience bigger things require.",
  "coupleChallenge40Category": "Relaxed",
  "coupleChallenge40Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge40Timing": "Afternoon",
  "coupleChallenge41Title": "A full day of gratitude",
  "coupleChallenge41Description": "Today's challenge: spend 24 hours without a single complaint. Every time someone complains, they have to balance it with something they are grateful for.\n\nAt the end of the day, go over all the good things you noticed.",
  "coupleChallenge41Motivation": "Changing the focus can change the entire relationship.",
  "coupleChallenge41Category": "Emotional",
  "coupleChallenge41Location": "Anywhere",
  "coupleChallenge41Timing": "All day",
  "coupleChallenge42Title": "Time capsule",
  "coupleChallenge42Description": "Choose five objects that represent your present: a photo, a ticket, a note. Put them in a box and seal it with a future opening date.\n\nWrite a letter to your future selves describing how you feel today.",
  "coupleChallenge42Motivation": "Saving the present is a gift you leave for the future.",
  "coupleChallenge42Category": "Emotional",
  "coupleChallenge42Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge42Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge43Title": "Blind painting",
  "coupleChallenge43Description": "One person covers their eyes and the other guides them with their voice to draw lines and colors on a sheet of paper. Then switch roles.\n\nTrust each other's voice and laugh at the abstract result you created together.",
  "coupleChallenge43Motivation": "Love can be painted with your eyes closed too.",
  "coupleChallenge43Category": "Playful",
  "coupleChallenge43Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge43Timing": "Anytime",
  "coupleChallenge44Title": "Our own podcast",
  "coupleChallenge44Description": "Record yourselves talking as if you were hosting a podcast. Pick a theme: your story, a trip, or what love has taught you.\n\nDo not try to sound perfect. Try to sound real. Keep it as a little voice capsule.",
  "coupleChallenge44Motivation": "Recording the voice of love is a way of keeping a living memory.",
  "coupleChallenge44Category": "Creative",
  "coupleChallenge44Location": "Quiet place",
  "coupleChallenge44Timing": "Anytime",
  "coupleChallenge45Title": "Delayed messages",
  "coupleChallenge45Description": "Each of you writes a letter to the other, but do not read them now. Exchange them and choose a date one week from now to open them.\n\nEnjoy the sweet waiting and the comfort of knowing a love message is waiting for you.",
  "coupleChallenge45Motivation": "Love can also be written in delayed time.",
  "coupleChallenge45Category": "Emotional",
  "coupleChallenge45Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge45Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge46Title": "Projection of memories",
  "coupleChallenge46Description": "Look for photos, videos, and messages from when you first met. Watch together how much you have grown and which obstacles you have overcome.\n\nRediscover the path that brought you to today.",
  "coupleChallenge46Motivation": "Looking back is one of the best ways to value the present.",
  "coupleChallenge46Category": "Emotional",
  "coupleChallenge46Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge46Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge47Title": "The yes day",
  "coupleChallenge47Description": "For one whole day, the rule is to say yes to every reasonable proposal the other person makes: ice cream, a walk, a nap.\n\nLet yourselves be carried by the flow of a day without noes.",
  "coupleChallenge47Motivation": "Too much structure wears you down. Flow brings you closer.",
  "coupleChallenge47Category": "Playful",
  "coupleChallenge47Location": "Anywhere",
  "coupleChallenge47Timing": "All day",
  "coupleChallenge48Title": "Toast to the future",
  "coupleChallenge48Description": "Prepare your favorite drink and make a toast while looking each other in the eyes. Write down one intention for the next chapter: a trip or a shared goal.\n\nSeal the toast with a smile that says, \"thank you for being here.\"",
  "coupleChallenge48Motivation": "Toasting what is coming is a way of honoring what you already are.",
  "coupleChallenge48Category": "Emotional",
  "coupleChallenge48Location": "Anywhere",
  "coupleChallenge48Timing": "Night",
  "coupleChallenge49Title": "Experimental cooking",
  "coupleChallenge49Description": "Choose three random ingredients you already have at home and try to create a brand-new dish together.\n\nNo looking up recipes. Use your instincts, taste as you go, and laugh if the experiment gets weird.",
  "coupleChallenge49Motivation": "Improvised flavor always carries something special.",
  "coupleChallenge49Category": "Creative",
  "coupleChallenge49Location": "Kitchen",
  "coupleChallenge49Timing": "Lunch/Dinner",
  "coupleChallenge50Title": "Wall of wishes",
  "coupleChallenge50Description": "Stick notes with wishes, gratitude, or goals on a wall or mirror. Let the wall grow throughout the week.\n\nRead every note at the end and keep them as witnesses of your intentions.",
  "coupleChallenge50Motivation": "Making a desire visible is the first step toward making it real.",
  "coupleChallenge50Category": "Thoughtful",
  "coupleChallenge50Location": "At home",
  "coupleChallenge50Timing": "All week",
